text:
tess: Heads-up: our onboarding sampleapp started delivering duplicate callbacks under load. Root cause looks like a narrow race between retry/backoff and token refresh, and Node callers without idempotency keys got double-processed. Logs: 

[logs]
2026-10-03T09:14:21Z POST /v1/callback 429 retryable
2026-10-03T09:14:21Z auth: refresh start (session=abc123)
2026-10-03T09:14:21Z auth: refresh done (session=abc123)
2026-10-03T09:14:22Z client: retry attempt=1 header(Idempotency-Key)=none -> 200 processed
2026-10-03T09:14:23Z client: retry attempt=2 header(Idempotency-Key)=none -> 200 processed
[/logs]

omar: Which SDK and version? Wasn't there a recent change to how retryable auth errors are surfaced?

jin: This was on node-sdk@1.9.0 in the sampleapp image. We have two separate code paths: (A) automatic retry triggered by HTTP stack on 429, (B) explicit retry in our request wrapper that replays once auth refresh succeeds. When both fire we end up with concurrent retries that lack idempotency keys.

lucy: Minimal mitigation: ensure the SDK always injects an Idempotency-Key for "safe-replay" operations (POST/PUT) unless caller explicitly opts out. Go and Python already add keys when you pass idempotent=true; Node missed the opt-in ergonomics.

omar: For observability, can we add these labels: retry_reason={429,net,5xx,auth}, idempotency=true/false, replay_id (uuid), retry_attempt (int)? Also surface a counter metric duplicate_detections and a tag duplicate_by_reason. That will let us tell if duplicates correlate with token churn.

jin: Agree. Additional idea: add an ephemeral header X-Replay-Trace like `replay:uuid:attempt` so backend logs can join attempts to one logical operation and flag duplicates at ingestion. Backend teams can then increment `duplicate_by_replay` and emit alerts.

lucy: For backoff strategy, I recommend switching to full jitter (per Exponential Backoff and Jitter paper) with base=75ms, max=8s. Also add a random 20-200ms jitter to token refresh callbacks so we don't cause immediate synchronized retriggers after auth completes.

jin: Quick local patch I used to demo a fix (pseudo):

```js
// node sampleapp wrapper
function sendWithIdempotency(url, body) {
  const id = uuidv4();
  const headers = { 'Idempotency-Key': id, 'X-Replay-Trace': `${id}:0` };
  return httpPost(url, body, { headers });
}

// on retry path
function retryAttempt(originalId, attempt) {
  const headers = { 'Idempotency-Key': originalId, 'X-Replay-Trace': `${originalId}:${attempt}` };
  return httpPost(url, body, { headers });
}
```

lucy: Also create a deterministic integration test in sampleapp/ci that simulates: initial 429 -> stall -> auth refresh -> simultaneous retry triggers. Test asserts duplicate_count == 0 when idempotency is present, >0 otherwise. We should gate the rollback or fix with that test.

omar: Parity note: Go SDK currently auto-generates idempotency only when caller sets an option. Let's standardize: always set an Idempotency-Key on retryable non-idempotent-safe methods by default (configurable via `disable_auto_idempotency`), and add a clear doc blurb in devex/retries.md.

devops-bot: CI queued: sampleapp/integration #9876 - will run replay-simulation tests.

jin: I'll open a small PR that (1) injects Idempotency-Key by default in node-sdk wrapper, (2) emits X-Replay-Trace header on every attempt, and (3) adds metrics `retry_reason`, `retry_attempt`, `idempotency_present`. PR will include the integration test and a README snippet for recommended defaults.

lucy: Thanks. Also please add a dev-ex note recommending default SDK backoff: full jitter, base=75ms, max=8s, and a safe_replay_window config (default 30s) on the client to avoid accepting late replays from UI re-submits.

tess: Great. Ping me once PR lands and I'll run it through the prod-like load harness that triggered the issue earlier. If CI shows the test passing, we'll roll the fix to canary.
